earlier_text:
Company Secretary

The role of the Company Secretary is outsourced to Levitt Kirson Business Services (Pty) Ltd, which meets the requirements of the Companies Act and the JSE.

The duties of the Company Secretary include:

u Providing counsel and guidance to the Board on their individual and collective powers and duties as required from time to time;

u Considering the regulatory universe prepared by internal audit and providing the Board with updates and proposed changes to laws and regulations affecting the Group;

u Reporting to the Board any non-compliance with the MOI or Companies Act;

u Maintaining proper minutes of shareholder, director and committee meetings;

u Certifying in the annual financial statements that the Company has filed the required notice and returns timeously in accordance with the Companies Act;

u Ensuring that the Company’s annual financial statements are properly distributed; and

u Carrying out the other functions required of a Company Secretary by the Companies Act.

The Board has considered and satisfied itself of the competence, qualifications and experience of the Company Secretary. More particularly, the Board is satisfied that the required duties have been carried out effectively.

The Board confirms that the Company Secretary has maintained an arm’s length relationship with the Board, is not a director of the Company and performs no other functions on behalf of the Company or the Board.

